    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i manage a rental property in phoenix and one of the tenants is complaining that their central AC is running all the time but one of the bedrooms stays really warm. the rest of the house seems fine. what are some common reasons why just one room wouldn't be getting enough cool air?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Several reasons could cause a single room with the central AC to remain warm. First, there might be a duct leak or blockage in that specific room, restricting airflow. Another possibility is that the thermostat for the AC unit may be incorrectly set to a higher temperature only for that room, or there may be an air leak around windows or doors. Additionally, the AC unit itself, located somewhere else, may be overheating or performing suboptimally. It's best to have a professional HVAC technician inspect the situation.",
      "source": "target",
