      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, it's quite plausible that something got stuck inside the ducts or there could even be an infestation of insects or rodents, which is more common in older homes or those with poor maintenance. Debris like dust, pet hair, or nesting material can accumulate and restrict airflow over time. Sealing all possible entry points for pests and conducting regular duct cleaning can mitigate these issues. It is highly recommended to have a professional HVAC technician assess the situation to address these duct-related concerns accurately.",
